#
# thrd_nomem and thrd_error from cnd_init() cannot be forced and are not
# tested. Waiters use the wt helper (atomic counters only).

assertion  XSH.cnd_init.001
anchor     functions/cnd_destroy.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/cnd_destroy.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       cnd_init() returns thrd_success; the condition variable can be
           destroyed with cnd_destroy().
test       t/001-init.c

assertion  XSH.cnd_init.002
anchor     functions/cnd_destroy.html#DESCRIPTION
class      disputed
since      2024
says       A thread that calls cnd_wait() on a newly initialized condition
           variable blocks: with no signal sent, it has not returned 300 ms
           later; it returns thrd_success once cnd_broadcast() is called.
note       disputed (Q-157): the page says the wait shall block, while
           cnd_wait() may return early for an unspecified reason (spurious
           wakeup); a return with nothing signalled is read here as not
           blocking.
test       t/002-fresh-blocks.c

assertion  XSH.cnd_init.003
anchor     functions/cnd_destroy.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/cnd_destroy.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       cnd_destroy() of an initialized condition variable with no waiters
           is safe; cnd_init() then succeeds on it again, and a waiter on it
           is woken by cnd_signal().
test       t/003-reinit.c
